<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher's static app shortcut — §9.2 of product_vision/06-emotional-journal.md.

  One long-press on the home-screen icon, one tap, and the journal opens with the check-in
  composer already up. There is no widget and no background process behind it: a shortcut is
  a row in this file, resolved by the launcher, and the only thing it does is start the
  activity the launcher would have started anyway with one extra piece of information.

  Static rather than dynamic (ShortcutManager) on purpose. A dynamic shortcut is published by
  code at runtime, which means a background component deciding what the launcher shows and
  keeping it in step; this is a resource, it is right from the first launch, it survives an
  app that has never been opened, and it needs no native code of any kind.

  The intent is explicit — targetPackage and targetClass name this app's own activity — so no
  <intent-filter> is added to the manifest for it. Adding one would make the scheme reachable
  from any browser and any other app, which is a wider door than a home-screen shortcut needs.
  Capacitor's App plugin fires `appUrlOpen` for an ACTION_VIEW intent carrying data whether or
  not a filter matched it, and `src/mobile/deepLink.js` accepts the URL only if it is one of
  the two this app itself declared.

  The scheme is Capacitor's `custom_url_scheme`, which is the application id; the rest is the
  route, and `src/constants/journal.js`'s JOURNAL_RECORD_PATH is the same string on the other
  side. `record=1` **arms** the composer — the recording starts on the confirming tap inside
  it, never on the launch.

  Deliberately one shortcut and not two. The nightly ritual has its notification (§3.6) and
  its place in the app; a second row here would be a second nudge in the one surface Android
  gives an app on the home screen, and §3.6's rule about the two nudges is the same rule.
-->
<shortcuts xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <shortcut
        android:shortcutId="journal-checkin"
        android:enabled="true"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:shortcutShortLabel="@string/shortcut_checkin_short_label"
        android:shortcutLongLabel="@string/shortcut_checkin_long_label">
        <intent
            android:action="android.intent.action.VIEW"
            android:targetPackage="com.thinkmusic.alexithymia"
            android:targetClass="com.thinkmusic.alexithymia.MainActivity"
            android:data="com.thinkmusic.alexithymia://journal?record=1" />
    </shortcut>
</shortcuts>
